From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Poyu Chen <me@poyu.xyz>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 06:01:45 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] bus: ti-sysc: do not clk_put() a devm-managed child clock

sysc_add_named_clock_from_child() gets the clock with
devm_get_clk_from_child() and then calls clk_put() on it, so devres puts
it a second time when the probe fails or defers later. This corrupts the
clock list (oops in __clk_put(), seen with the OMAP4 McPDM pdmclk).

Upstream: not submitted
---
 drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c | 7 ++++++-
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c b/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c
index f715c8d28..65b6a50c4 100644
--- a/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c
+++ b/drivers/bus/ti-sysc.c
@@ -362,7 +362,12 @@ static int sysc_add_named_clock_from_child(struct sysc *ddata,
 	cl->clk = clock;
 	clkdev_add(cl);
 
-	clk_put(clock);
+	/*
+	 * No clk_put() here: the clock came from devm_get_clk_from_child() and
+	 * is released by devres. Putting it here as well makes devres put it a
+	 * second time when the probe fails or defers later (hlist corruption in
+	 * __clk_put(), seen on the WT41N0 with the McPDM pdmclk).
+	 */
 
 	return 0;
 }
